# orgsync

`orgsync` is a small command-line tool that reconciles the work items held by a
Directory service with the accounts held by a Ledger service and keeps a
per-owner summary in the Ledger up to date, writing what it did to `out/`. It
uses the Python standard library only. The two service base URLs are read from
`config.json`, which the environment provisions; run `python3 -m orgsync
--help` for the available commands and `python3 -m unittest discover
tests/existing` for the test suite that ships with the package.
